{"id":"000VWR","title":"Taken at Face Value","author":"greyden","solvedCount":3,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T11:02:13+00:00","posted":"Heute, 09:26 Uhr","rules":"Taken at Face Value\n\nRules:\n\n1. Normal Sudoku Rules Apply. Place the digits 1 to 9 once in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\n2. Killer Cages. Values in cages sum to the number in the top left corner of the cage.\n\n3. Changed Values of Digits. All of the digits 1 to 9 have had their values altered in one of four ways. Each of the nine digits are either halved, doubled, squared, or multiplied by -1. Values are globally consistent; for example, if you deduce a 9 is squared, then all 9s are squared.\n\n4. Tracking Table. The tracking table contains rows for indicating deduced tens, units, and decimal point values. For example, if 3 is halved to have a value of 1.5, place a 1 in the units row under 3, and a 5 in the decimal row under 3. If a value is negative, you don't need to indicate that it is negative in the tracking table.\n\n5. Fog of War. Most of the grid and tracking table is covered in fog. Placing correct digits may clear some fog. No guessing is required. The tracking table is synced to the fog mechanics and needs to be filled in too. On completion of the puzzle, the solution code for Logic Masters Germany is revealed between the puzzle and tracking table.\n\nSolve on Sven's SudokuPad\n\nPlease Enjoy!","solutionCode":"Solution Code is given in the puzzle on completion.","tags":["Sudoku","Killer (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/7gayoe3mza","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/7gayoe3mza","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":14,"cols":9,"cages":17,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T11:02:13+00:00"}